# Repo-root .dockerignore — used when a Waypoint image build's context is the repo
# root (issue #92: backend/Dockerfile now builds from here so it can see .editorconfig
# and Directory.Build.props). Keep this lean and keep local/secret material out of every
# build context, same intent as .gitignore's "NEVER commit" list in CLAUDE.md — a
# .dockerignore miss ships the file INTO the image layer, which is worse than a git miss
# because it can leave a running host, not just a repo.
#
# Only the paths a Dockerfile actually needs should reach the daemon. backend/Dockerfile
# COPYs Directory.Build.props, .editorconfig, and backend/ explicitly, so everything
# else at the repo root is excluded by default here and re-included per-Dockerfile only
# if a future image needs it.

# Version control / editor / CI metadata — never needed inside a build.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local secrets & operator config (mirrors .gitignore — CLAUDE.md "NEVER commit"):
# gitignored dev material must not leak into an image even though .dockerignore and
# .gitignore are evaluated independently and a gitignore entry alone does NOT stop
# Docker from sending a file to the daemon.
.env
.env.*
*.token
*.vault
vault-pass*
secrets*.json
secrets*.yml
/config/
dev/local/
*.local.json
*.local.yml
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12

# Build/dependency output — large, regenerated inside the build, never a build input.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
frontend/build/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Docs and other components not needed by the backend image build. Re-include per
# Dockerfile if a future image genuinely needs one of these (e.g. a frontend image
# would need an exception for frontend/ — add it there, not by loosening this file).
docs/
frontend/
scripts/
README.md
